{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/thm-skew-poisson-integrates","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:skew-poisson-integrates","kind":"theorem","title":"Integration theorem","uses":["papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-commutative-formal-group","papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-skewed-poisson-structure","papers/fred2005-formal-groups/blocks/def-non-commutative-formal-group"],"cites":["references/fred2005"],"tags":["integration","formal-group","main-theorem"],"leanRef":"fred2005:Fred2005.skew_poisson_integrates","text":"skew-poisson-integrates.md","leanSource":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/skew-poisson-integrates.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:skew-poisson-integrates\"></a><p><strong>Integration theorem</strong> (<span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"fred2005\">[fred2005]</span>, Main Theorem):\nA <a href=\"#def:skewed-poisson-structure\">skewed-Poisson structure</a> on a\n<a href=\"#def:commutative-formal-group\">commutative formal group</a> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H / \\mathbb{F}_p</code>\nintegrates to a <a href=\"#def:non-commutative-formal-group\">non-commutative formal group</a>\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G / \\mathbb{Z}_p</code>.</p>\n<p>The construction uses <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}(H)</code> as the distribution algebra,\nthe formal group law deformed by the bracket as multiplication,\nand the diagonal as comultiplication (group-like elements).</p>\n","source":"folio/fred2005-formal-groups/formal-groups-chapter/skew-poisson-integrates.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Theorem","number":"1.3.2"}
